<h1>Install metais</h1>

<p><code>metais</code> is one static binary with no dependencies.</p>

<table>
<thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>Route</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>macOS</td><td><a href="#homebrew">Homebrew</a>: <code>brew install kottera/tap/metais</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Linux, or a Mac without Homebrew</td><td><a href="#script">The install script</a>: <code>curl -fsSL https://metais.org/install.sh | sh</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Go users</td><td><a href="#go">Go</a>: <code>go install metais.org/metais/cmd/metais@latest</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Anyone</td><td><a href="#release">The release's archives</a> and <code>SHA256SUMS</code></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<p>Every route but <code>go install</code> installs the same bytes: the
archives of the release on GitHub. <code>go install</code> builds the same
version from the module.</p>

<h2 id="homebrew">Homebrew</h2>

<pre><code>brew install kottera/tap/metais</code></pre>

<h2 id="script">The install script</h2>

<pre><code>curl -fsSL https://metais.org/install.sh | sh</code></pre>

<p><a href="/install.sh">install.sh</a> is a short POSIX shell script; read
it before you run it. It runs on macOS and Linux, on amd64 and arm64. It
downloads this machine's archive and <code>SHA256SUMS</code> from the GitHub
release, and refuses to install unless the archive's SHA-256 is the one
<code>SHA256SUMS</code> lists for it.</p>

<p>It installs <code>metais</code> into <code>~/.local/bin</code>, or into
the directory <code>METAIS_INSTALL_DIR</code> names, with no
<code>sudo</code>. It never edits your shell's startup files: when the
directory is not on your <code>PATH</code>, it says so and prints the line
to add to one.</p>

<pre><code>curl -fsSL https://metais.org/install.sh | METAIS_INSTALL_DIR=/opt/metais/bin sh</code></pre>

<p>Without <code>METAIS_VERSION</code>, it installs the latest release that
is not a prerelease. <code>METAIS_VERSION</code> pins a version, with or
without its leading <code>v</code>:</p>

<pre><code>curl -fsSL https://metais.org/install.sh | METAIS_VERSION=1.0.0 sh</code></pre>

<h2 id="go">Go</h2>

<pre><code>go install metais.org/metais/cmd/metais@latest</code></pre>

<h2 id="release">The release's archives</h2>
{%- if release.published %}

<p>metais {{ release.version }}, from the release
<a href="https://github.com/kottera/metais/releases/tag/{{ release.tag }}">{{ release.tag }}</a>,
and its <a href="{{ release.sums_url }}"><code>SHA256SUMS</code></a>:</p>

<table class="archives">
<thead><tr><th>Archive</th><th>SHA-256</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{%- for a in release.archives %}
<tr><td><a href="{{ a.url }}"><code>{{ a.name }}</code></a></td><td><code>{{ a.sha256 }}</code></td></tr>
{%- endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{%- else %}

<p>Download the archive for your platform,
<code>metais_&lt;version&gt;_&lt;os&gt;_&lt;arch&gt;.tar.gz</code>, and
<code>SHA256SUMS</code> from
<a href="https://github.com/kottera/metais/releases/latest">the latest release</a>.</p>
{%- endif %}

<p>Verify the archive against <code>SHA256SUMS</code> in the directory that
holds both, on Linux and on macOS:</p>

<pre><code>sha256sum --check --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS
shasum -a 256 --check --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS</code></pre>

<p>Each prints the archive's name and <code>OK</code>. Then unpack
<code>metais</code> into a directory on your <code>PATH</code>:</p>

<pre><code>tar -xzf metais_*_linux_amd64.tar.gz metais
mkdir -p ~/.local/bin
mv metais ~/.local/bin/</code></pre>

<p>On macOS, a binary downloaded with a browser carries the quarantine
attribute, and Gatekeeper refuses to run it. Remove it after you have
verified the archive:</p>

<pre><code>xattr -d com.apple.quarantine ~/.local/bin/metais</code></pre>

<h2 id="next">Next</h2>

<pre><code>metais version
metais skill</code></pre>

<p><code>metais version</code> prints the version you installed.
<a href="/reference/commands/skill/"><code>metais skill</code></a>, run at
the top of a project, gives the project's coding agent the skill that
teaches it metais.</p>
